{
  "rules": [
    "Systematic Underestimation of Bullish Spikes: The model consistently fails to capture upward price surges (e.g., the rise to ~76 EUR), forecasting a flat or slightly declining trend while true outcomes spike. Correction: Apply a positive bias adjustment when sentiment history shows consecutive high values (>= 0.67) or when recent price momentum is strongly positive.",
    "Excessive Mean Reversion Lag: Forecasts revert to the mean too quickly after a spike, missing the sustained high plateau. Correction: Extend the duration of the elevated price level in the forecast horizon by 3-5 days following a breakout, rather than immediately reverting to the historical average.",
    "Sentiment-Price Decoupling: High sentiment scores (1.00) are not weighted sufficiently in the model, leading to forecasts that ignore bullish signals. Correction: Increase the forecast slope multiplier when the average sentiment over the last 3 days exceeds 0.67.",
    "Over-correction on Downside: The model predicts a steady decline that is too aggressive compared to the actual volatility, often missing the floor or the subsequent bounce. Correction: Flatten the downward slope in the forecast when sentiment drops to 0.00 but recent history shows resilience (prices not breaking previous lows)."
  ]
}
